<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ -1 \end{array}\right)}</m> and <m>\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ -5 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(a) Find <m>{-3}\mathbf{a}</m>.</p><div><m>{-3}\mathbf{a} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>{2}\mathbf{a} - {2}\mathbf{b}</m>.</p><div><m>{2}\mathbf{a} - {2}\mathbf{b} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>A scalar multiplies every component; it never adds to them.</p><p>(a) Multiply each component by <m>{-3}</m>: <m>{-3}\mathbf{a} = {-3}{\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ -1 \end{array}\right)} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 12 \\ 3 \end{array}\right)}</m>. The scalar is negative, so the vector is reversed: both signs change.</p><p>(b) <m>{2}\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -8 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)}</m> and <m>{-2}\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 4 \\ 10 \end{array}\right)}</m>. Add matching components: <m>{2}\mathbf{a} - {2}\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 8 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 12 \\ 3 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 8 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>